      "source_page": 9
    }
  ],
  "notes": "Modified cash basis audit (village), FYE 9/30/2023. Governmental: General, Street, Debt Service (Totals column p5). Fund balances 470,571 -> 525,719 (p6) roll forward; cash (cash and cash equivalents + cash held by county treasurer) from the governmental funds statement p4: 2023 Total 343,019, 2022 comparative Total 409,955 (cash differs from fund balance by due from/to other funds). Taxes 260,609 split by printed breakdown: General Fund combining schedule p10 (property 71,403, motor vehicle 10,687, sales 35,357, franchise 56,185 incl. Fire 1,178), Statement of Activities p7 (property taxes for debt service 59,258) and the Street Fund remainder 27,719 = SoA franchise fees 83,904 - 56,185. The p5 'Transfers out' 966 is printed positive (inflow) in the General Fund and matches the Ambulance fund's (966) on p8: recorded as transfers_in. Capital outlay 43,106 mixes Street 32,500, Fire 2,606 and Park 8,000. Business-type from the modified cash proprietary statement p8 (Totals column); it ties to the Statement of Activities business-type expenses 405,561 (p2), the printed business-type disbursement total used; measure = cash as in FY2024 (modified cash net position: cash 289,970 less due to other funds 182,700). Capital expenses and debt service printed as nonoperating expenses are recorded as positive disbursements. Balance sheet = government-wide Statement of Net Position (p1), because it has internal balances (the funds statement shows due to/from other funds instead); liabilities printed '-0-'. Detail: General Fund combining schedule p10 by department column; Street and Debt Service from the p5 fund columns; Sewer, Ambulance, Water, Sanitation from the p8 columns. The p9 combined budget-and-actual schedule (single all-funds column, includes Nursing Home lines not in the statements) was not recorded to avoid double counting; see decision_needed. Read pages 1-10 of 10"
}
